      { kind: "text", text: "Piles, or haemorrhoids, are swollen blood vessels and supporting tissue in or around the anal canal. They may be internal, external or mixed. Many cases improve with dietary changes, bowel-habit correction and medicines, while persistent or advanced haemorrhoids may require a procedure." }
